---
const agents = ["Claude Code", "Codex", "OpenCode", "Pi", "Grok Build"];
---

<section id="agents" class="section">
  <div class="wrap grid">
    <div>
      <h2 class="heading">Your agent, inside your notes.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Open a CLI you already use in the side panel, on the login you already have. Logia doesn't touch your credentials.
        The note you have open goes along with each message, unsaved edits included, and you can leave it out.
      </p>

      <ul class="agents">{agents.map((name) => <li>{name}</li>)}</ul>

      <ul class="points">
        <li><b>Edits land live.</b> Agents write through the running app, into the same editor and save queue you use.</li>
        <li><b>Your typing wins.</b> A full rewrite must quote the note's revision. If the note changed, it's rejected.</li>
        <li><b>Permissions stay yours.</b> Each CLI keeps its own settings, and Logia adds no bypass flags.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="term" role="img" aria-label="Terminal example: an agent searches, appends to a note, and has a stale rewrite rejected">
      <div class="term-head"><span>logia-cli</span><span>talks to the running app</span></div>
      <pre><code><span class="c"># see the note, unsaved edits included</span>
<span class="p">$</span> logia-cli read

<span class="c"># find something across your notes</span>
<span class="p">$</span> logia-cli search query="meeting notes"

<span class="c"># add to a note; it appears as you watch</span>
<span class="p">$</span> logia-cli append file="Plan" content="- [ ] Review"

<span class="c"># replace it, but only if nothing has changed</span>
<span class="p">$</span> logia-cli write id=NOTE_ID ifRevision=REVISION --stdin
&#123; "error": &#123; "code": "<span class="e">REVISION_CONFLICT</span>",
             "message": "Note changed. Read it again before editing." &#125; &#125;</code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .section {
    padding-block: clamp(64px, 10vw, 120px);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ink-800);
    background: var(--ink-950);
  }

  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.08fr);
    gap: clamp(32px, 5vw, 72px);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .lede {
    margin-top: 14px;
  }

  .agents {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px;
    margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .agents li {
    padding: 4px 10px;
    border: 1px solid var(--ink-800);
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: var(--ink-900);
    color: var(--ink-200);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .points {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-top: 28px;
    color: var(--ink-400);
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .points b {
    color: var(--ink-100);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .term {
    min-width: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--ink-800);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--ink-925);
  }

  .term-head {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 10px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink-800);
    color: var(--ink-500);
    font: 400 12px/1.3 var(--mono);
  }

  pre {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 18px 16px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    color: var(--ink-100);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .c {
    color: var(--ink-500);
  }

  .p {
    color: var(--ember-400);
  }

  .e {
    color: var(--ember-300);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 920px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
